# The hero's right-facing stand: the other half of a named mirror.
#
# Found by a sweep for named pieces whose opposite-direction twin is NOT
# named -- the generalisation of the crouch case in crouch_poses.map, where
# a half-named mirror turned out to be invisible in every count.
#
# HERO_STAND_LEFT_BODY and HERO_STAND_LEFT_ARM were named; nothing was named
# HERO_STAND_RIGHT_*. The mirror is LABEL_7955 in CAPSULE, and it has the
# same three components in the same order as the left-facing routine:
#
#   left                                   right (LABEL_7955)
#   call DRAW_HERO_WATER_DEPTH_LEFT_...    call DRAW_HERO_WATER_DEPTH_RIGHT_...
#   video HERO_STAND_LEFT_BODY             video CV_0F90
#   jne [0x0A] -> HERO_GUN_ARM_POSE_LEFT   jne [0x0A] -> HERO_GUN_ARM_POSE_
#   video HERO_STAND_LEFT_ARM              video CV_338E
#
# Geometry confirms the pairing without reference to the routine:
#
#   HERO_STAND_LEFT_BODY  41.0 tall, 6 leaves, top -40.5
#   CV_0F90               41.0 tall, 6 leaves, top -40.5
#   HERO_STAND_LEFT_ARM   15.0 tall, 1 leaf,   top -35.5
#   CV_338E               16.0 tall, 1 leaf,   top -35.0
#
# Both drawn at [HERO_X] only, neither behind a guard.
CV_0F90 HERO_STAND_RIGHT_BODY
CV_338E HERO_STAND_RIGHT_ARM
